WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.810
RYAN MATSUMOTO: Today we're
talking about GKE image

00:00:02.810 --> 00:00:04.910
streaming, Student
Success Services,

00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:06.870
and 5G network slicing.

00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:09.740
I'm Ryan, and welcome to "This
Week in Cloud," where we serve

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:12.050
you the lowest-latency news.

00:00:12.050 --> 00:00:14.210
We're excited to announce
the general availability

00:00:14.210 --> 00:00:16.610
of a new feature in
Google Kubernetes Engine--

00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:17.840
image streaming.

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:20.690
This revolutionary GKE
feature has the potential

00:00:20.690 --> 00:00:23.630
to drastically improve your
application scale-up time,

00:00:23.630 --> 00:00:25.730
allowing you to respond
to increased user demand

00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:28.100
more rapidly and save
money by provisioning

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:29.720
less spare capacity.

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:31.970
We achieve this by
reducing the image pull

00:00:31.970 --> 00:00:34.190
time for your container
from several minutes,

00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:37.160
in the case of large images,
to a couple of seconds,

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:40.400
irrespective of container size,
and allowing your application

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:43.340
to start booting immediately
while GKE streams the container

00:00:43.340 --> 00:00:45.140
data in parallel.

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:47.900
A recent survey found
that 87% of companies

00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:50.090
reported that they are
now experiencing skills

00:00:50.090 --> 00:00:52.670
gaps now or in the coming year.

00:00:52.670 --> 00:00:54.650
And the impact of
the pandemic has only

00:00:54.650 --> 00:00:57.590
added to the urgency for
schools and education-technology

00:00:57.590 --> 00:01:01.490
companies to find new ways to
support even more learners.

00:01:01.490 --> 00:01:04.190
To meet these challenges and
scale specialized learning

00:01:04.190 --> 00:01:06.440
across more students
globally, we

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:09.590
are expanding our portfolio
of Student Success Services

00:01:09.590 --> 00:01:12.380
with a new Google Cloud
artificial intelligence-powered

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:15.920
learning platform, which
features the Interactive Tutor.

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:18.410
This platform will provide
new ways for educators

00:01:18.410 --> 00:01:21.350
to share curriculum and will
bring more on-demand learning

00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:23.870
opportunities to students.

00:01:23.870 --> 00:01:26.930
Building on the recent releases
of the Android 12 operating

00:01:26.930 --> 00:01:29.330
system and Google
Distributed Cloud,

00:01:29.330 --> 00:01:31.730
Google is paving the way
for communication service

00:01:31.730 --> 00:01:33.800
providers, as well
as enterprises,

00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:36.560
to deliver enterprise
applications and services

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:40.620
over 5G network slices for
enhanced application security,

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:42.780
reliability, and performance.

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:45.890
5G network slicing enables
virtual mobile networks

00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:49.220
to be created dynamically with
varying properties utilizing

00:01:49.220 --> 00:01:51.680
shared underlying
physical resources.

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:54.860
5G slicing is one of the
key areas of innovations

00:01:54.860 --> 00:01:58.490
that will let CSPs earn a return
on their investments in 5G

00:01:58.490 --> 00:02:00.830
by offering a secure
and dynamic network

00:02:00.830 --> 00:02:02.917
platform to enterprises.

00:02:02.917 --> 00:02:05.000
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:07.440
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:08.690
Any thoughts or ideas?

00:02:08.690 --> 00:02:10.509
Leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:02:10.509 --> 00:02:12.970
We'll see you in the cloud.

